      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Prometheus metrics power the charts above and contain aggregate counts by severity, workload, image tag and digest. **They do not include individual CVE IDs or package names.** Those details are stored in Trivy `VulnerabilityReport` custom resources.\n\n```bash\n# List report names and namespaces\nkubectl get vulnerabilityreports -A\n\n# Show full CVEs, affected package, installed/fixed versions, score and advisory links\nkubectl get vulnerabilityreport <report-name> -n <namespace> -o json | jq '.report.vulnerabilities[] | {severity, vulnerabilityID, title, package: .resource, installedVersion, fixedVersion, score, primaryLink}'\n\n# Export all reports as TSV for sorting / spreadsheet review\nkubectl get vulnerabilityreports -A -o json | jq -r '.items[] as $r | $r.report.vulnerabilities[] | [$r.metadata.namespace,$r.metadata.name,.severity,.vulnerabilityID,.title,.resource,.installedVersion,.fixedVersion,(.score // \"\"),.primaryLink] | @tsv'\n\n# Inspect a configuration audit finding or an exposed-secret report\nkubectl get configauditreports -A\nkubectl get exposedsecretreports -A\nkubectl describe configauditreport <report-name> -n <namespace>\n```\n\nMatch report names to the workload and namespace in the tables above. Secret reports may contain sensitive paths or values; do not paste their contents into tickets or chat."
      }
